{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793003952,"nonce":"YNB1kz+GlcPSsrWkUCb6eUMrPs4=","title":"Generic property keys lose enum-abstract arguments during reactive conversion","message":"The ImagePreview.hx probe still reports valid Node.set(Prop.Position, Position.Absolute) and Single arguments as mismatches after the separate macro transport-signature fix. A native rayzor.toml project reduces it to the following source. The LSP reports expected Key\u003cT\u003e, found Key\u003cMode\u003e and expected Reactive\u003cT\u003e, found Reactive\u003cInt\u003e on the Mode call; the Single call passes. The hover on Key.Position correctly retains Key\u003cMode\u003e, so this is call inference/conversion rather than hover formatting.\n\n```haxe\nenum abstract Mode(Int) to Int { var Absolute = 1; }\nabstract Key\u003cT\u003e(Int) {\n  public static inline var Position:Key\u003cMode\u003e = cast 1;\n  public static inline var Width:Key\u003cSingle\u003e = cast 2;\n}\nenum ReactiveValue\u003cT\u003e { Const(value:T); }\nabstract Reactive\u003cT\u003e(ReactiveValue\u003cT\u003e) from ReactiveValue\u003cT\u003e {\n  @:from public static inline function fromConst\u003cT\u003e(value:T):Reactive\u003cT\u003e return Const(value);\n  @:from public static inline function fromInt(value:Int):Reactive\u003cSingle\u003e return Const((value:Single));\n}\nclass Target {\n  public function new() {}\n  public function set\u003cT\u003e(key:Key\u003cT\u003e, value:Reactive\u003cT\u003e):Void {}\n}\nclass Main {\n  static function main() {\n    var target = new Target();\n    target.set(Key.Position, Mode.Absolute);\n    target.set(Key.Width, (1:Single));\n  }\n}\n```\n\nUse a rayzor.toml with [project] name=\"generic-key-probe\" and [cache] enabled=false. The declaration of the generic key must determine the payload type before choosing an implicit conversion; an enum abstract that converts to Int must retain its nominal type as the key payload. Add positive and negative LSP/session and compiler checks. The related MIR-only conversion issue is 4c1d8fb1ee528cd700a0ea915f4bf59e1fa1985b42332606da1a851b77787a70, which should not be treated as evidence that this typer failure is fixed. Current probe: /tmp/rayzor-lsp-markup-review/generic.log.","files":null}]}